    "text": "To round \\(\\frac{4}{7}\\) to the nearest tenth, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the fraction to a decimal:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{7} \\approx 0.5714285714285714\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the digit in the tenths place:**\n   The decimal \\(0.5714285714285714\\) has the digit 5 in the tenths place.\n\n3. **Identify the digit in the hundredths place:**\n   The digit immediately to the right of the tenths place (in the hundredths place) is 7.\n\n4. **Determine whether to round up or down:**\n   - If the digit in the hundredths place is 5 or greater, we round up the digit in the tenths place.\n   - If the digit in the hundredths place is less than 5, we round down (keep the digit in the tenths place the same).\n\n   Here, the digit in the hundredths place is 7, which is greater than 5. Therefore, we round up the digit in the tenths place from 5 to 6.\n\n5. **Form the rounded number:**\n   The number \\(0.5714285714285714\\) rounded to the nearest tenth is \\(0.6\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.6}\n\\]",
